      "panels": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": 14,
          "title": "How kured patching works here",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 17,
            "w": 24,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 37
          },
          "options": {
            "mode": "markdown",
            "content": "**Schedule.** unattended-upgrades installs security updates daily at 01:30. kured reboots only on **Sunday 02:00-06:00 (Asia/Singapore)**, one node at a time, and only nodes whose running kernel or CPU microcode is out of date. Expect ~15 minutes per node.\n\n**Annotations** (toggle them at the top of the dashboard; hover a marker for details):\n- **Kernel update** (green): the node came back on a new kernel. Shows before -> after and a changelog link.\n- **Microcode update** (purple): the node came back with new CPU microcode.\n- **Reboot, nothing updated** (red): a reboot with no kernel or microcode change: a power cut, crash or manual reboot.\n- **Reboot became required** (yellow): a new kernel was installed and is waiting for Sunday.\n- **Cordoned** (orange): kured holds the lock and is draining that node.\n\n**If a node is stuck orange (cordoned):** the drain cannot evict a pod. Find it and check for PDBs with 0 disruptions allowed:\n```\nkubectl -n kube-system logs -l app.kubernetes.io/name=kured --since=1h | grep -E \"Draining|evict|Unable\"\nkubectl get pdb -A -o custom-columns=NS:.metadata.namespace,NAME:.metadata.name,ALLOWED:.status.disruptionsAllowed\n```\n\n**Who holds the reboot lock** (lockTtl is 0, so it never expires on its own):\n```\nkubectl -n kube-system get ds kured -o jsonpath='{.metadata.annotations.weave\\.works/kured-node-lock}'\n```\nOnly once that node is back and Ready, clear it by hand: `kubectl -n kube-system annotate ds kured weave.works/kured-node-lock-`\n\n**Exactly what changed on a node** (all packages, not just the kernel): `grep -A20 \"$(date +%F)\" /var/log/apt/history.log` or `journalctl -u apt-daily-upgrade --since -7d`.\n\nFull background: `apps/kured/values.yaml`.\n",
            "code": {
              "language": "shell",
              "showLineNumbers": false,
              "showMiniMap": false
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
